# PHASE 5 — Language comprehension profiles

Do not build separate applications for different languages.

Create prompt/profile behavior.

## German profile

My High German is functional but not fluent.

Help especially with:

* idioms;
* slang;
* subtleties;
* humor;
* wordplay;
* culturally dependent references;
* difficult constructions.

Prefer explanations that help me improve my German rather than replacing all German with English.

English should be available as a fallback.

## Swiss German

My Swiss German is very poor.

Relatives generally switch to High German when addressing me, but speak Swiss German among themselves.

Test specialized Swiss-German ASR models and, where useful:

Swiss German speech
→ Standard German transcription
→ optional explanation/English

## French profile

I am fluent in French.

Do NOT waste attention translating normal French or explaining long-established elementary idioms.

My primary weakness is:

* newly coined slang;
* recently fashionable expressions;
* current catchphrases;
* contemporary cultural references;
* ironic/new meanings;
* expressions that may have appeared only recently.

Design the architecture so current slang knowledge can eventually be refreshed independently of the base local model.

A future freshness mechanism may perform an on-demand external lookup of only the unfamiliar phrase, rather than transmitting surrounding conversation.

Do not implement external lookup until the local system is solid.

